# 10. ESTABLISH GIT AND CHANGE MANAGEMENT

Prepare the project for version control.

Use Git.

Establish:
- Meaningful commit conventions.
- Feature branches where appropriate.
- Code review procedures.
- Safe rollback procedures.
- Secret management.
- A useful .gitignore.
- Repository documentation.

Never commit:
- Passwords.
- API keys.
- Private credentials.
- Production secrets.
- Sensitive user data.

Use .env.example to document required environment variables without exposing actual secrets.

Inspect Git changes before committing.

Never perform destructive Git operations without explicit approval.

